Both verifiers independently found the compaction bridge broken in ways a
green suite (43 certification + 5 golden, tripwire 5/5) could not see.

Dispatched now (independent of Lee's ruling): E0 two undeclared core
touchpoints (lhc_inference.rs + session/mod.rs:331 — unmarked, absent from
FORK.md's 'every owned core line'; placement ruled acceptable, the silence was
not; renumber to n/6); E1 replace_compact runs twice per logical event and the
bridge's fail-open verdict is silently reverted by run_compact_only, so native
never compacts after announcing it would; E2 disabled path clones the whole
conversation and emits a WARN every turn for users who never enabled LHC;
E3 inference uses the primary model not a dedicated one, snapshots credentials
at spawn (native compaction re-resolves because tokens expire), has no
cancellation, discards all LHC target fields, and string-matches errors;
E4 hook 4 awaits the capture worker with no timeout on the request path;
E5 tests asserting constants against themselves — including the ONLY
prompt_index test, while translated messages are built with
ConversationItem::user which carries no prompt_index at all;
E6 no test invokes either compact path; E7 fmt red.

ESCALATED to Lee (stop line 2 — both need new core touchpoints or move a host
contract, neither is decide-and-proceed):
1. Serving coverage: /btw recap sends 'the parent session's full context' as
   an independent request bypassing hook 4, as does memory-flush. Verified in
   recap.rs:9,36,108. Partial serving diverges intermittently.
2. Replace-mode accounting: hook 5 suppresses the native writer, which was the
   only thing that ever lowered total_tokens — so the threshold stays tripped,
   LHC compacts every turn forever, /context climbs past 100%, and hook 4's
   fail-open path sends an oversized native body. The two hooks are
   individually defensible and jointly broken.

Replace mode is to be treated as unreachable pending that ruling.

